From fc226252baea54391d39a8eb60dd1c4d89ada41e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerome Tollet <jtollet@cisco.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:02:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] nvmf: allow requests to extend I/O vectors

Some transports can receive a payload in more segments than fit in the
request's inline iovec array. Increasing the inline array penalizes every
request, including transports and workloads that never need the extra
capacity.

Add an optional transport-owned extended iovec and accessors for the
active vector and its capacity. Keep the existing 33-entry inline array
as the default and update common NVMf paths to use the active vector.

Change-Id: Iacf1a63a2609d595cb103941cf4e086824b89314
Signed-off-by: Jerome Tollet <jtollet@cisco.com>
---
